# Reviewed exceptions to the dependency (SCA) gate.
#
# The Trivy gate deliberately does NOT set `ignore-unfixed`, so a CRITICAL or
# HIGH with no upstream patch available blocks the merge instead of passing
# silently. This file is the escape hatch for that case — but it is a
# per-vulnerability, reviewed decision, not a blanket exemption.
#
# Every entry must record why it is safe to ignore and when it expires, e.g.:
#
#   # CVE-2024-00000 — prototype pollution in <pkg>. No fix released upstream.
#   # Not reachable: the affected API (<fn>) is never called from this app.
#   # Re-review by 2026-12-01 (tracked in issue #NN).
#   CVE-2024-00000 exp:2026-12-01
#
# An entry without a rationale and an expiry date should not pass review.
#
# Currently empty: the dependency tree has no CRITICAL/HIGH findings.
